{#
  An evidence review document: one or more cases in one HTML file.

  One case per file is this phase's output. The same template over a longer
  ``vm.cases`` is the supplementary document a later phase assembles, so there
  is nothing to restructure then — only the collection's front matter to fill.
#}<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8"/>
<meta content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" name="viewport"/>
<title>{{ vm.title }}</title>
<style>
{% include "_evidence.css.j2" %}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
{#
  A publication page says what it is before anything else on it. The footer
  states the transform in full and must stay there, but a footnote is read
  last, or not at all: a page lifted into a slide, a figure or a printed
  bundle arrives with transformed values and no indication of it. This band
  travels with the first thing a reader sees.

  Deliberately a band and not a tint behind the text: a diagonal wash over a
  page of tables is what print engines drop and screen readers never had, and
  the one claim this page must not lose is this one. For the same reason it
  says MASKED and not "anonymised" — what ran is a transform, and whether the
  result may be released is a disclosure reviewer's conclusion. The line under
  the word says *select* values, because that is what is true: a transform may
  leave a value as reported, and a band claiming everything had moved would be
  the one piece of publication metadata a reader cannot check. What this run
  actually did, and the caveat that the page is not certified anonymised, are
  in the footer, which is written from the effective policy.
#}
  {#
    One case, so the band belongs here: first element inside <main>, which is
    what makes it survive a screenshot or a crop. A collection draws one per
    example instead — see _evidence_case.html.j2 — because every example
    opens a sheet and a band here would sit alone on the cover sheet.
  #}
  {% if vm.mode.value == 'publication' and vm.cases | length == 1 %}
  <div class="masked-banner" role="note">
    {#- The word is capitalised in the markup, not only by CSS: a copy
       of this page with its stylesheet stripped, or any reader taking the
       text, must still carry it. -#}
    <span class="masked-word">MASKED</span>
    <span class="masked-detail">Select displayed values have been
    transformed.</span>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
{#
  The heading is skipped when a single case already carries its own title:
  the case's own <h2> is then the document's heading, and printing both would
  show the same words twice. A collection always gets the heading, because its
  title names the collection rather than any one case.
#}
  {% set single_titled = vm.cases | length == 1 and vm.cases[0].title %}
  {% if not single_titled %}
  {% if vm.cases | length > 1 %}<div class="kicker">Evidence review</div>{% endif %}
  <h1>{{ vm.title }}</h1>
  {% endif %}
  {% if vm.intro %}<p class="intro">{{ vm.intro }}</p>{% endif %}
  {% if vm.note %}<p class="note">{{ vm.note }}</p>{% endif %}

  {% for case in vm.cases %}
  {% include "_evidence_case.html.j2" %}
  {% endfor %}

  <footer>
    {{ (vm.provenance.lines or ['vigiTwin']) | join(' · ') }} ·
    llm_dup_dev.review_html, evidence format{% if vm.generated_at %} · rendered {{ vm.generated_at }}{% endif %}.
    <br/>
    {% if vm.mode.value == 'publication' %}
    {#
      What was transformed comes from the run, not from this template: the
      policy is configurable, and a footer naming every attribute category
      would be wrong for any run that left one of them as reported.
    #}
    Prepared for publication.
    {{ vm.transform_note or "Displayed values have been transformed, and the
    assessments, scores, contributions and penalties are those of the
    original reports." }}
    {% if vm.approved_for_release %}
    {#
      Said only on the strength of a signed, pinned release: the candidate
      wording is the default because the candidate state is the safe one.
      The manifest beside this page says the same thing, and a test holds
      the two to the same phrase.
    #}
    Cleared for public sharing by the study's disclosure reviewer.
    {% else %}
    A candidate for disclosure review, not a document certified as
    anonymised.
    {% endif %}
    {% else %}
    This is an internal evidence review. It may contain original report
    identifiers, country names and narrative text, and is not a
    publication-safe document.
    {% endif %}
  </footer>
</main>
{#
  The repeating per-sheet footer, for paper. A sheet lifted out of a printed
  bundle carries neither the MASKED band nor the footer above, both of which
  appear once per document; this is the one claim that travels with every
  sheet. Static text: Chrome paints a fixed element once per page but reaches
  neither @page margin boxes nor counter(page), so there is no page number
  here and cannot be. Outside <main> so no `main > *` rule can reach it, and
  outside <style> so the rendered scan reads it like any other markup.
#}
<div class="page-footer">
  {%- if vm.mode.value == 'publication' -%}
    {%- if vm.approved_for_release -%}
      {#-
        The title, like a running head, and then the one claim a released
        sheet must not lose. Being cleared for publication settles the
        disclosure question and leaves the interpretive one: a reader must
        not take a shifted date for a real one, and on a loose sheet this is
        the only place that says so.
      -#}
      {{ vm.title }} — displayed values transformed.
    {%- else -%}
      Candidate for disclosure review — displayed values transformed, not
      certified as anonymised.
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    Internal evidence review — may contain original identifiers and narrative
    text. Not publication-safe.
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
</body>
</html>
